  "facts": [
    "The Bronx–Whitestone Bridge, designed by Othmar Ammann and Allston Dana, opened on April 29, 1939, initially with four lanes and a sleek Art Deco I‑beam deck that later received stiffening trusses after the Tacoma Narrows collapse.",
    "With a 2,300‑foot main span and towers 377 feet tall, the bridge once boasted the fourth‑largest suspension span worldwide, its cables totaling 14,800 miles of wire—more than the length of the Earth’s equator.",
    "Renovated from 1988 to 1991 and again in the mid‑2000s, the bridge’s deck, approach viaducts, and anchorages were replaced, and the stiffening trusses were removed to restore its original streamlined appearance."
  ],
